<mujoco model="xarm6_pusht_shelf_gap">
  <!-- Push the T between two shelves -- open_table plus two large static
       blocks that leave a gap between them.

       IsaacGym conf/task/sim_task03.yaml, re-scaled onto the lab table and
       the measured T-block (see tee.xml's header).

       THE GAP IS THE TASK, so it is sized against the T rather than in
       absolute metres. It is now 0.200 m -- 2.2 T-crossbars, up from the
       0.1335 m (1.5x) squeeze -- centred on x = 0.381, the corridor's own
       x, so straight through stays the centred route.

       The shelves run PARALLEL TO THE ARM (long axis along x, the reach
       direction) and are shorter and smaller than before: 0.26 x 0.16 x
       0.14 m and 0.10 x 0.16 x 0.14 m, against the 0.14 x 0.25 x 0.20 m
       they were. The far one hugs the far table edge at x = 0.75, closing
       that bypass outright. The near one CANNOT hug the near edge -- the
       arm is bolted to it, at the origin -- so it stops at x = 0.19,
       0.099 m clear of the 0.0912 m base shell, and what is left between
       the base and it is a 0.099 m slot: passable by the 0.089 m crossbar
       with 1 cm to spare, which keeps "go around the outside" alive as a
       genuinely tighter alternative to the gap.

       The gate sits at y = 0, dead centre of the table and 0.4 m from
       both ends of the corridor, so the block starts and finishes well
       clear of it.

       oim/utils/scenes.py carries the matching Boxes; tests/test_scenes.py
       fails if the two drift apart. -->
  <include file="common.xml"/>
  <include file="tee.xml"/>
  <include file="tee_start.xml"/>

  <worldbody>
    <!-- Own camera, steeper than the other three tabletop scenes': at the
         shared elevation=-25 the shelves block the view of the gap and the
         pusher between them, even though nothing falls outside the frame --
         elevation dropped to -60 fixes that. Same azimuth=180 and
         distance=1.30 as the shared camera, with the lookat translated
         +0.045 along the camera's own right axis (world +y at azimuth=180)
         to bring the arm closer to frame centre: lookat (0.381, 0.045,
         0.10) instead of the shared (0.381, 0, 0.10). -->
    <camera name="front" pos="1.0310 0.0450 1.2258"
      xyaxes="0.0000 1.0000 0.0000 -0.8660 0.0000 0.5000"/>

    <geom class="tabletop_obstacle" name="shelf_1" type="box" size="0.13 0.08 0.07" pos="0.62 0.0 0.07"/>
    <geom class="tabletop_obstacle" name="shelf_2" type="box" size="0.05 0.08 0.07" pos="0.24 0.0 0.07"/>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
